Article 7 A foreign law firm applying to establish a representative office in China and to dispatch representatives shall meet the following conditions:
(1) The foreign law firm has been legally practicing in its home country and has not been punished for violating lawyers' professional ethics or practice discipline;
(2) The representative of the representative office shall be a practicing lawyer and a member of the bar association of the country where the practice qualification is obtained, and shall have practiced outside China for not less than two years, and shall not have been subjected to criminal punishment or punished for violating lawyers' professional ethics or practice discipline; among them, the chief representative shall have practiced outside China for not less than three years and shall be a partner of the foreign law firm or a person holding an equivalent position;
(3) There is an actual need for establishing a representative office in China to carry out legal services business.

Article 8 A foreign law firm applying to establish a representative office in China shall submit the following documents and materials to the judicial administration department of the people's government of the province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government where the proposed representative office is to be located:
(1) A written application signed by the principal person in charge of the foreign law firm for the establishment of the representative office and the dispatch of representatives. The name of the proposed representative office shall be "XX Law Firm (Chinese translation of the law firm's name) Representative Office in XX (name of Chinese city)";
(2) A certificate evidencing the legal establishment of the foreign law firm in its home country;
(3) The partnership agreement or founding charter of the foreign law firm, along with a list of its persons in charge and partners;
(4) The power of attorney granted by the foreign law firm to each proposed representative of the representative office, and a confirmation that the proposed chief representative is a partner of the law firm or a person holding an equivalent position;
(5) Certificates evidencing the lawyer's practice qualification of each proposed representative of the representative office and that the proposed chief representative has practiced outside China for not less than three years and other proposed representatives have practiced outside China for not less than two years;
(6) Certificates issued by the bar association of the country where the foreign law firm is located, evidencing that each proposed representative of the representative office is a member of that bar association;
(7) Certificates issued by the lawyer management authority of the country where the foreign law firm is located, evidencing that neither the law firm nor any proposed representative has been subjected to criminal punishment or punished for violating lawyers' professional ethics or practice discipline.
The documents and materials listed in the preceding paragraph shall be notarized by a notarial institution or notary in the applicant's home country, authenticated by the competent foreign affairs authority of that country or an authority authorized thereby, and certified by the embassy or consulate of China in that country. Where the international treaties concluded or acceded to by China provide otherwise, the certification procedures specified in such international treaties shall be followed.
The documents and materials submitted by the foreign law firm shall be in triplicate, and documents in foreign languages shall be accompanied by Chinese translations.

Article 13 Where a representative of a representative office is in any of the following circumstances, the judicial administration department of the State Council shall revoke his or her practice permit and recover his or her practice certificate, and the judicial administration department of the people's government of the province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government shall accordingly cancel his or her practice registration:
(1) The lawyer's practice license in his or her home country has become invalid;
(2) His or her representative status has been revoked by the foreign law firm to which he or she belongs;
(3) His or her practice certificate or the practice license of the representative office where he or she works has been lawfully revoked.

Article 14 Where a representative office is in any of the following circumstances, the judicial administration department of the State Council shall revoke its practice permit and recover its practice license, and the judicial administration department of the people's government of the province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government shall accordingly cancel its practice registration:
(1) The foreign law firm to which it belongs has been dissolved or cancelled;
(2) The foreign law firm to which it belongs has applied for its cancellation;
(3) It has ceased to meet the conditions specified in Article 7 of these Regulations;
(4) Its practice license has been lawfully revoked.
A representative office that is cancelled in accordance with the preceding paragraph shall conduct liquidation according to law; before the debts are fully settled, its property shall not be transferred out of China.

Article 15 A representative office and its representatives may only engage in the following activities that do not involve Chinese legal affairs:
(1) Providing clients with advice on the laws of the country where the lawyers of the foreign law firm are authorized to practice, as well as advice on relevant international treaties and international practices;
(2) Accepting entrustment by clients or Chinese law firms to handle legal affairs in the country where the lawyers of the foreign law firm are authorized to practice;
(3) Representing foreign clients in entrusting Chinese law firms to handle Chinese legal affairs;
(4) Handling legal affairs by maintaining a long-term entrustment relationship with Chinese law firms through concluding contracts;
(5) Providing information on the impact of the Chinese legal environment.
In accordance with the agreements reached with Chinese law firms, a representative office may directly make requests to the lawyers of the entrusted Chinese law firms.
A representative office and its representatives shall not engage in any legal services activities or other profit-making activities other than those specified in paragraphs 1 and 2 of this Article.

Article 17 In their practice activities, a representative office and its representatives shall not commit any of the following acts:
(1) Providing false evidence, concealing facts, or threatening or inducing others to provide false evidence, conceal facts, or obstructing the opposing party from lawfully obtaining evidence;
(2) Taking advantage of the convenience of legal services to accept property or other benefits from a party;
(3) Disclosing the trade secrets or personal privacy of a party.

Article 22 A representative office shall, before March 31 each year, submit to the judicial administration department of the people's government of the province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government where it is domiciled the copies of the practice license and the practice certificates of the representatives, as well as the following inspection materials for the preceding year, to undergo annual inspection:
(1) The circumstances of carrying out legal services activities, including the circumstances of entrusting Chinese law firms to handle legal affairs;
(2) The annual financial statements of the representative office audited by an accounting firm, and the vouchers for settlement within China and tax payment according to law;
(3) The changes in representatives of the representative office and the employment of Chinese assistants;
(4) The residence of the representatives of the representative office within China;
(5) The registration status of the representative office and its representatives;
(6) Other circumstances of fulfilling the obligations specified in these Regulations.
After conducting annual inspection of the representative offices set up within its administrative region, the judicial administration department of the people's government of the province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government shall submit the inspection opinions to the judicial administration department of the State Council for recordation.

Article 26 Where a representative office is in any of the following circumstances, the judicial administration department of the people's government of the province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government shall give it a warning and order it to make corrections within a time limit; if the circumstances are serious, the said department shall order it to suspend operations within a time limit; if it fails to make corrections within the time limit, the judicial administration department of the State Council shall revoke its practice license:
(1) Employing Chinese practicing lawyers, or employing assistants to provide legal services;
(2) Failing to settle within China the fees collected for carrying out legal services;
(3) Failing to submit annual inspection materials on time for annual inspection, or failing to pass the annual inspection.
Where there is any illegal act listed in subparagraph (2) of the preceding paragraph, the judicial administration department of the people's government of the province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government shall impose a fine of not less than one time but not more than three times the amount that should have been settled within China.

Article 27 Where a representative office or a representative is in any of the following circumstances, the judicial administration department of the people's government of the province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government shall give it a warning and confiscate the illegal gains; if the circumstances are serious, it shall order it to suspend operations within a time limit and impose a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan:
(1) Serving or concurrently serving as a representative in more than one representative office;
(2) Disclosing the trade secrets or personal privacy of a party;
(3) Taking advantage of the convenience of legal services to accept property or other benefits from a party.

Article 32 Where a staff member of the judicial administration department commits any of the following illegal acts, the responsible persons in charge and other directly responsible persons shall be given administrative sanctions of recording a demerit, recording a major demerit, or demotion according to law:
(1) Failing to examine or review the certifying documents and materials of a proposed representative office or proposed representative in accordance with the conditions specified in these Regulations;
(2) Failing to register or conduct annual inspection of a representative office in accordance with the provisions of these Regulations;
(3) Charging fees not in accordance with the fee items and fee standards prescribed by the State.

Article 33 Where a staff member of the judicial administration department commits any of the following illegal acts, the responsible persons in charge and other directly responsible persons shall be given administrative sanctions of demotion, removal from office, or expulsion according to law:
(1) Deciding to issue a practice license or practice certificate to a proposed representative office or proposed representative that does not meet the conditions specified in these Regulations;
(2) Taking advantage of his or her position to accept property or seek private gains;
(3) Violating the provisions of these Regulations by failing to revoke the practice permit of a representative office or representative that should be revoked, or failing to recover the practice license or practice certificate, or failing to cancel the practice registration that should be cancelled;
(4) Failing to issue a receipt for fines collected according to law or failing to truthfully fill in the amount of fine;
(5) Failing to implement the system of separating the decision on fines from the collection of fines, or failing to turn over to the national treasury all fees collected according to law, fines collected and illegal gains confiscated according to the provisions;
(6) Failing to promptly investigate and deal with acts of a representative office or representative violating the provisions of these Regulations;
(7) Other acts of not strictly enforcing the law or abusing power, causing serious consequences.
Where any of the illegal acts listed in the preceding paragraph causes serious losses to public property, the State or the interests of the people, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law in accordance with the provisions of the Criminal Law on the crime of abuse of power, the crime of dereliction of duty, or the crime of accepting bribes.
